WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.822
AI red teaming should be guided by threat models and risk priorities.

2
00:00:03.822 --> 00:00:18.159
Teams may test prompt injection, indirect prompt injection, data leakage, unsafe tool use, harmful outputs, retrieval failures, excessive permissions, overreliance, or weak human oversight.

3
00:00:18.159 --> 00:00:28.736
Clear objectives help testers focus on risks that matter to the organization instead of running random experiments that produce interesting but unactionable results.

4
00:00:28.736 --> 00:00:35.640
A good objective names the scenario, system component, expected evidence, and decision the team wants to support.

5
00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.539
Threat modeling also helps distinguish model-level issues from system-level issues.

6
00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:50.686
The same observed behavior may have different severity depending on what the system can access, what actions it can take, and what review exists before impact occurs.

7
00:00:50.686 --> 00:00:53.550
Objectives should be realistic and defensible.

8
00:00:53.550 --> 00:01:02.869
The team should understand the business context, user roles, data sensitivity, expected workflows, and control assumptions that make a scenario important.
